  "body": "Distinct dyadic profiles can have exactly equal roots under the actual count-dependent bit surcharge, leaving a safe interval comparison unresolved. This package completes PR1508's explicit surcharge-equality handoff: for m=2^k, dyadic ranks, positive integer stock and admitted nonnegative integer counts, it retains lambda=32m^2/10^16 and proves that the roots agree exactly when the monic polynomial GCD is negative at one. Otherwise rational brackets eventually separate. Counts and rank masses may differ.\n\nThe package includes direct-source-residual certificate checks independent of the primary polynomial compiler/GCD, unequal-count rational and irrational ties, a shared-negative-root counterexample, and a constant-GCD pair requiring 684 refinements. The unchanged pinned PR1392 signed-price routine is actually executed on both ties with assertions enabled, retaining its correct unresolved intervals. The polynomial GCD and bisection are standard techniques already present in PR1508; the new coverage is the actual surcharge contract and complete equality decision, not a claim that either predecessor is wrong.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Registered Python3.12.7 replay passes all 9,669 profile pairs, reverse checks, six named fixtures, 16 semantic controls and six end-to-end integrity tests.\n- Optimized Python3.14.5 recomputes the identical complete receipt. A separate AI reviewer inspected the proof, source normalization and certificate logic, then independently passed the optimized Python3.12.14 replay.\n- Source SHA256/Git blobs are checked before predecessor execution; Git-free export, altered executable source, typed/incomplete receipt and overwrite controls pass. Fresh main and predecessor heads remain unchanged; recent REST overlap supplements the older complete Discussion snapshot (GraphQL rate-limited).\n\nReproduce: `python3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/surcharged-dyadic-comparator`.\n\nScope is arithmetic only. It does not integrate PR1392's fixed PR589 caller, whose idle rank42 is non-dyadic, or claim physical circuit realizability, supplier adoption, efficient worst-case separation, a complete invoice, selected cold replay or new kappa. Recursive hosting, precision/tape, bit H1-H5, hosted CI and independent human review remain unrun. The next question is a real caller whose entire profiles satisfy the exact branch's contract while preserving its replication/idle normalization.\n\nPrepared by ywz65 with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in derivation, implementation, verification and writing. Credit Hanson Sun (@bbMisk)/PR1508 for the unsurcharged comparator and explicit handoff; Brian Ross/PR1392 for retained-fee reference pricing; flemhhh/PR1048 for original interval routines; woklerx/PR1182 for endpoint repair; Douglas Colkitt for the existing fixed-exponent counterexample. Exact predecessor notices and licenses are retained. New work is Apache-2.0.\n",
